hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17852","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Layth, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn Abi Habib, that he heard Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Zubaydi say: I am the first who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None of you shall urinate facing the qiblah, and I am the first who conveyed that to the people."
"17853","Al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid, meaning Ibn Ja'far, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' al-Zubaydi, he said: I am the first of the Muslims who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding that one urinate facing the qiblah, so I went out to the people and informed them."
"17854","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' al-Zubaydi, he said: We ate roast meat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque, then prayer was established, so we put our hands into the pebbles, then stood and prayed and did not perform ablution."
"17855","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ziyad al-Hadrami narrated to us that he heard Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' al-Zubaydi, companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us that one of us urinate facing the qiblah."
"17856","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Mughirah, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' say: I did not see anyone who smiled more than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"17857","Harun narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I heard it myself from Harun, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Haywah ibn Shurayh informed me, he said: 'Uqbah ibn Muslim informed me, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' al-Zubaydi, he said: We were one day with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Suffah, and food was placed for us and we ate, then prayer was established, so we prayed and did not perform ablution."
"17858","Harun narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Haywah narrated to me, from 'Uqbah ibn Muslim al-Tujibi, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' al-Zubaydi, from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: Woe to the heels and the bellies of the feet from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection. Abdullah said: And he did not raise it [to the Prophet]. Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from Harun."
"17859","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us that he heard Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Zubaydi say: I am the first who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None of you shall urinate facing the qiblah, and I am the first who conveyed that to the people."
"17860","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Mughirah, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' al-Zubaydi informed me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: None of you shall urinate facing the qiblah, and I am the first who conveyed that to the people."
"17861","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Abi 'Imran and Sulayman ibn Ziyad al-Hadrami, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' al-Zubaydi, he said: We ate roast meat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque, then prayer was established, so we struck our hands in the pebbles, then stood and prayed and did not perform ablution."
"17862","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from 'Uqbah ibn Muslim, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' al-Zubaydi, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the heels and the bellies of the feet from the Fire."
"17863","Harun narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us: 'Amr narrated to us that Sulayman ibn Ziyad al-Hadrami narrated to him that Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' al-Zubaydi narrated to him that he and a companion of his passed by Ayman and a group of Quraysh who had loosened their waist-wrappers and made them into whips, striking one another with them while naked. Abdullah said: When we passed by them, they said: These are priests, so leave them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to them, and when they saw him they scattered. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned angry until he entered, and I was behind the chamber, and I heard him say: Glory be to Allah, neither from Allah did they feel shame nor from His Messenger did they veil themselves. And Umm Ayman was with him, saying: Seek forgiveness for them, O Messenger of Allah. Abdullah said: With difficulty did he seek forgiveness for them. Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from Harun."
"17864","Musa ibn Dawud and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, and Hasan ibn Musa said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Darraj, Musa said in his hadith, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' al-Zubaydi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed in Hellfire are snakes like the necks of Bukht camels; one of them stings the sting, and he finds its heat for forty autumns. And indeed in Hellfire are scorpions like saddled mules; one of them stings the sting, and he finds its heat for forty years."
"17865","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Mughirah, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' al-Zubaydi, he said: I did not see anyone who smiled more than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"17866","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Mughirah, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' al-Zubaydi, he said: I did not see anyone who smiled more than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"17867","Musa narrated to us: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' al-Zubaydi, he said: I am the first who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None of you shall urinate facing the qiblah, and I am the first who conveyed that to the people."
